<title>FRANCE: ALPINE SKIING-FRITZ STROBL WINS VAL D'ISERE MEN'S DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-FRITZ STROBL WINS VAL D'ISERE MEN'S DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>VAL D'ISERE, France 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Fritz Strobl won a men's World Cup Alpine skiing downhill on Sunday in a time of one minute 51.61 seconds.</p>
<p>Fellow Austrians Werner Franz and Patrick Ortlieb  were second and third on 1:51.63 and 1:51.72 respectively.</p>
